refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
boolopcache_invalidate stringfilename boolforce&false;
This function invalidates a particular script from the opcode cache. If force is unset or &false;, the script will only be invalidated if the modification time of the script is newer than the cached opcodes. If the opcache.file_cache directive is enabled, this function also invalidates the corresponding file cache entry.
Avoid calling this function with untrusted input. When the opcache.file_cache directive is enabled and
opcache.file_cache_read_only is not enabled, a filename that starts with one or more ../ can escape from the opcache file cache directory and allow deleting any file ending in .bin that the user has permission to delete. This includes files that open_basedir might otherwise limit access to.
